{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":5,"lang":"pl","title":"Czyje to","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Czego się nauczysz","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W tej lekcji uczysz się mówić, kto co ma i czyje coś jest: «mam brata», «to mój kubek», «kask jest mój», «kubek męża», «czyja to klawiatura?». Po angielsku służy do tego kilka różnych słówek."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"She has a brother.","translation":"Ona ma brata.","hi":"has"},{"en":"This is my mug.","translation":"To mój kubek.","hi":"my"},{"en":"The helmet is mine.","translation":"Kask jest mój.","hi":"mine"},{"en":"The mug is my husband's.","translation":"Kubek jest męża.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"Whose keyboard is this?","translation":"Czyja to klawiatura?","hi":"Whose"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"«Mam» — I have","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Tu polski pomaga: «mam klucz» to I have a key. Pamiętaj tylko o I na początku: po polsku «ja» znika, bo słychać je w «mam». Po angielsku Have a key bez I to niepełne zdanie."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"have / has","accent":true},{"text":"co","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I have a key.","translation":"Mam klucz.","hi":"have"},{"en":"We have a sister.","translation":"Mamy siostrę.","hi":"have"},{"en":"I have a computer.","translation":"Mam komputer.","hi":"have"},{"en":"They have wallets.","translation":"Mają portfele.","hi":"have"},{"en":"I have a guest.","translation":"Mam gościa.","hi":"have"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Have a key.","right":"I have a key."}]}]},{"num":"03","title":"have czy has","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Z he, she, it albo z jedną osobą czy rzeczą — has: she has, the hotel has. Ze wszystkimi innymi — have: I have, you have, we have, they have. To ta sama para co is i are."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"She has a baby.","translation":"Ona ma dziecko.","hi":"has"},{"en":"He has a cat.","translation":"On ma kota.","hi":"has"},{"en":"The hotel has a dog.","translation":"W hotelu jest pies.","hi":"has"},{"en":"The desk has paper.","translation":"Na biurku jest papier.","hi":"has"},{"en":"The twins have a dog.","translation":"Bliźniaki mają psa.","hi":"have"},{"en":"My nephew has a puppy.","translation":"Mój siostrzeniec ma szczeniaka.","hi":"has"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"She have a brother.","right":"She has a brother."},{"wrong":"I has a key.","right":"I have a key."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"She","after":"a baby.","options":["have","has","is"],"answer":"has","why":"Z she — has."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"my, your, his, her — przed rzeczą","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «mój kubek», «moja torba», «moje ołówki» — słowo zmienia się według rzeczy. Po angielsku my jest zawsze takie samo: my mug, my bag, my pencils. Liczy się tylko, czyja to rzecz."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This is my mug.","translation":"To mój kubek.","hi":"my"},{"en":"Your tissue is in my pocket.","translation":"Twoja chusteczka jest w mojej kieszeni.","hi":"Your"},{"en":"Her lunchbox is in the fridge.","translation":"Jej pudełko na lunch jest w lodówce.","hi":"Her"},{"en":"His tattoo is small.","translation":"Jego tatuaż jest mały.","hi":"His"},{"en":"These are my pencils.","translation":"To są moje ołówki.","hi":"my"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"This is mine mug.","right":"This is my mug."},{"wrong":"These are mys pencils.","right":"These are my pencils."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Polskiego «swój» po angielsku nie ma. Zamiast niego zawsze my, your, his, her — zależnie od tego, czyja to rzecz."}]},{"num":"05","title":"his czy her","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jak po polsku: «jego» i «jej» mówią o właścicielu. Rzecz mężczyzny — his, rzecz kobiety — her. Patrz na to, czyja to rzecz, a nie na samą rzecz."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"His tattoo is small.","translation":"Jego tatuaż jest mały.","hi":"His"},{"en":"Her ponytail is long.","translation":"Jej kucyk jest długi.","hi":"Her"},{"en":"This is her puppy.","translation":"To jej szczeniak.","hi":"her"},{"en":"It is her bookcase.","translation":"To jej regał.","hi":"her"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Mówisz o kucyku dziewczyny. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"His ponytail is long.","optionB":"Her ponytail is long.","correct":"B","explain":"Kucyk jest jej, więc her."}}]},{"num":"06","title":"our, their, its","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"our — «nasz», their — «ich». its — «jego» o rzeczy albo zwierzęciu: its collar — obroża szczeniaka. its piszemy bez apostrofu. It's z apostrofem to it is."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Our printer is next to the window.","translation":"Nasza drukarka stoi przy oknie.","hi":"Our"},{"en":"Its collar is red.","translation":"Jego obroża jest czerwona. *(szczeniaka)*","hi":"Its"},{"en":"Its tail is short.","translation":"Ma krótki ogon. *(szczeniak)*","hi":"Its"},{"en":"Where is my laptop?","translation":"Gdzie jest mój laptop?","hi":"my"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It's collar is red.","right":"Its collar is red."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Sprawdź: da się powiedzieć it is? To it's. Nie da się — its."}]},{"num":"07","title":"mine, yours, hers — kiedy rzecz już padła","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli rzecz już padła, «mój» idzie na koniec i ma inną formę: The helmet is mine. Porównaj: my helmet — «mój kask», ale The helmet is mine — «kask jest mój». Po mine rzeczy się nie powtarza."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"my → mine","accent":false},{"text":"your → yours","accent":false},{"text":"his → his","accent":false},{"text":"her → hers","accent":false},{"text":"our → ours","accent":false},{"text":"their → theirs","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"The helmet is mine.","translation":"Kask jest mój.","hi":"mine"},{"en":"The guitar is yours.","translation":"Gitara jest twoja.","hi":"yours"},{"en":"The razor is his.","translation":"Maszynka jest jego.","hi":"his"},{"en":"The perfume is hers.","translation":"Perfumy są jej.","hi":"hers"},{"en":"The kite is ours.","translation":"Latawiec jest nasz.","hi":"ours"},{"en":"The puzzle is theirs.","translation":"Puzzle są ich.","hi":"theirs"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"The helmet is my.","right":"The helmet is mine."},{"wrong":"The perfume is her.","right":"The perfume is hers."},{"wrong":"This is mine helmet.","right":"This is my helmet."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"The guitar is","after":".","options":["your","yours","you"],"answer":"yours","why":"Rzecz już padła, «twoja» na końcu — yours."}}]},{"num":"08","title":"Czyjaś rzecz: my husband's","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «kubek męża» — najpierw rzecz, potem czyja. Po angielsku odwrotnie: najpierw kto, potem co, a do osoby dodaje się 's: my husband's mug. Jeśli rzecz już padła, można jej nie powtarzać: The mug is my husband's."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"osoba + 's","accent":false},{"text":"rzecz","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"The mug is my husband's.","translation":"Kubek jest męża.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"This is my sister's thermos.","translation":"To termos mojej siostry.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"The dog is the neighbour's.","translation":"Pies jest sąsiada.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"My aunt's piano is old.","translation":"Pianino mojej cioci jest stare.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"The baby's bib is in my sister's bag.","translation":"Śliniak dziecka jest w torbie siostry.","hi":"'s"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"The thermos of my sister.","right":"My sister's thermos."},{"wrong":"This is thermos my sister's.","right":"This is my sister's thermos."},{"wrong":"The dog is the neighbour.","right":"The dog is the neighbour's."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Powiedz: «To termos mojej siostry».","answer":["This","is","my","sister's","thermos"],"distractors":["sister","of"]}}]},{"num":"09","title":"Whose — «czyj»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Żeby zapytać «czyj?», Whose idzie na sam początek, a zaraz za nim rzecz: Whose keyboard is this? Dla kilku rzeczy — are these: Whose gloves are these?"},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Whose","accent":true},{"text":"rzecz","accent":true},{"text":"is this / are these","accent":true},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Whose keyboard is this?","translation":"Czyja to klawiatura?","hi":"Whose"},{"en":"Whose gloves are these?","translation":"Czyje to rękawiczki?","hi":"Whose"},{"en":"Whose monitor is that?","translation":"Czyj to monitor? *(tamten)*","hi":"Whose"},{"en":"It is hers.","translation":"Jej.","hi":"hers"},{"en":"They are mine.","translation":"Moje.","hi":"mine"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Whose is this keyboard?","right":"Whose keyboard is this?"},{"wrong":"Who's keyboard is this?","right":"Whose keyboard is this?"},{"wrong":"Whose gloves is this?","right":"Whose gloves are these?"}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Who's i whose brzmią tak samo, ale who's to who is. «Czyj» piszemy zawsze whose."}]},{"num":"10","title":"Odpowiedź na «czyj?» — krótko","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Na Whose…? odpowiada się krótko: It is hers. They are mine. It is my brother's. Rzeczy się nie powtarza — padła już w pytaniu."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Whose badge is this? — It is mine.","translation":"Czyj to identyfikator? — Mój.","hi":"mine"},{"en":"Whose pendant is this? — It is hers.","translation":"Czyj to wisiorek? — Jej.","hi":"hers"},{"en":"Whose binoculars are these? — They are mine.","translation":"Czyja to lornetka? — Moja.","hi":"mine"},{"en":"Is this pendant yours? — No, it isn't mine.","translation":"To twój wisiorek? — Nie, nie mój.","hi":"isn't"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is my.","right":"It is mine."}]}]},{"num":"11","title":"Dwa rodzaje 's","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"my sister's bag — «torba siostry»: tu 's znaczy «czyj». A My cousin's here — «mój kuzyn jest tutaj»: tu 's to krótkie is. Łatwo odróżnić: jeśli po 's jest rzecz — to «czyj». Jeśli miejsce albo cecha — to is."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"My friend's flute is here.","translation":"Flet mojego przyjaciela jest tutaj.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"My cousin's here.","translation":"Mój kuzyn jest tutaj.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"The rabbit's bowl is empty.","translation":"Miska królika jest pusta.","hi":"'s"}]}]},{"num":"12","title":"Błędy, które robi prawie każdy","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Have a key.","right":"I have a key."},{"wrong":"She have a brother.","right":"She has a brother."},{"wrong":"This is mine mug.","right":"This is my mug."},{"wrong":"The helmet is my.","right":"The helmet is mine."},{"wrong":"It's collar is red.","right":"Its collar is red."},{"wrong":"The thermos of my sister.","right":"My sister's thermos."},{"wrong":"Whose is this keyboard?","right":"Whose keyboard is this?"}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Przed rzeczą — my, your, his, her, our, their. Bez rzeczy, na końcu — mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs. O osobie — 's: my sister's."},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Pokazujesz kask i mówisz, że jest twój. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"The helmet is my.","optionB":"The helmet is mine.","correct":"B","explain":"Na końcu, bez rzeczy — mine."}}]},{"num":"13","title":"Co zabrać do ćwiczeń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"«Mam» — I have, on i ona — has. «Mój kask» — my helmet, «kask jest mój» — the helmet is mine. «Siostry» — my sister's. «Czyj?» — Whose… is this? I its bez apostrofu — «jego» o rzeczy."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"He has a phone.","translation":"On ma telefon.","hi":"has"},{"en":"Her aunt is in the kitchen.","translation":"Jej ciocia jest w kuchni.","hi":"Her"},{"en":"The rackets are ours.","translation":"Rakiety są nasze.","hi":"ours"},{"en":"The saw is my uncle's.","translation":"Piła jest wujka.","hi":"'s"},{"en":"Whose trophy is this?","translation":"Czyj to puchar?","hi":"Whose"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{}}
